# Rust core rules

- Read `.agents/skills/css-doctor-core/SKILL.md` and `AGENTS.md`.
- Class matching is case-insensitive; any matching class marks a selector used
  by a page (conservative DCE).
- Selectors without classes are global → common.
- `coverage >= min_page_ratio` → common; `0` → dead; otherwise page-specific,
  copied to each using page.
- Keep `@font-face`, `@keyframes`, `@import` in common. Recursively split
  conditional at-rules and nested style rules.
- Use `BTreeMap`/`BTreeSet` for deterministic output; never panic on user input.
- Run `cargo fmt --all -- --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features
  -- -D warnings`, `cargo test`.
- If public types/functions change, update `packages/binding` and rebuild it.
